WEBVTT

00:25.734 --> 00:27.944
RESIDENT PLAYBOOK

00:29.529 --> 00:31.030
EPISODE 1

00:31.114 --> 00:31.948
BP is dropping.

00:32.032 --> 00:34.993
BP is 80 over 60. Heart rate is 130.
Respiration is 30.

00:35.076 --> 00:37.245
Start another line
in the other arm for fluid loading.

00:37.328 --> 00:38.705
-Yes, sir.
-Sir!

00:38.788 --> 00:41.124
Sir, open your eyes! Are you awake?

00:41.207 --> 00:43.043
Sir, can you hear me?

00:44.294 --> 00:45.420
Okay, let's move him.

00:45.503 --> 00:46.671
One, two, three!

00:47.172 --> 00:49.215
Sir, do you know where you are?

00:49.299 --> 00:50.633
Could you try opening your eyes?

00:50.717 --> 00:51.593
BP is dropping.

00:53.261 --> 00:54.471
Starting CPR.

00:57.140 --> 00:58.308
What's going on?

00:58.391 --> 01:00.643
TA patient, with mental status stupor,
went into arrest,

01:00.727 --> 01:01.853
so I'm performing CPR.

01:01.936 --> 01:03.063
-Open him up.
-Here?

01:03.772 --> 01:05.565
It'll be a table death
if we don't do it now.

01:05.648 --> 01:06.608
Open him up. Hurry.

01:07.192 --> 01:08.610
Wait. Me?

01:08.693 --> 01:11.279
-But I'm just an intern--
-Get it together!

01:16.076 --> 01:18.578
If we don't stop the internal bleeding,
he won't survive.

01:18.661 --> 01:19.496
Don't you know that?

01:22.999 --> 01:24.709
Don't just stand there! Do it now!

01:33.885 --> 01:37.639
We'll perform simultaneous surgeries.
I'll lower the intracranial pressure.

01:37.722 --> 01:40.558
Dr. Oh, perform cardiac massage
directly with your hands.

01:40.642 --> 01:43.436
But I don't even have gloves on.

01:43.520 --> 01:46.314
Does that matter right now?
That's not what's important.

01:46.397 --> 01:48.399
Then what is important?

01:48.483 --> 01:49.526
What's important is…

01:53.404 --> 01:55.240
You gave up being a doctor.

01:55.323 --> 01:56.616
You quit.

01:57.826 --> 01:58.868
You're

01:59.494 --> 02:00.703
not a doctor anymore.

02:22.350 --> 02:23.768
You gave up being a doctor.

02:23.852 --> 02:24.853
You quit.

02:24.936 --> 02:28.815
You're not even a doctor.
What are you even doing here?

02:28.898 --> 02:30.817
Oh Yi-young, you're not a doctor.

02:30.900 --> 02:33.069
-Ms. Oh?
-Dr. Oh.

02:33.153 --> 02:34.946
-Ms. Oh?
-Dr. Oh!

02:35.029 --> 02:36.197
Ms. Oh?

02:41.119 --> 02:42.287
Are you okay?

02:44.914 --> 02:46.249
You must've been dreaming.

02:46.332 --> 02:48.960
Yes, it was a nightmare.

02:49.043 --> 02:50.086
Oh, dear.

02:51.880 --> 02:54.048
Geez, I just had to dream
something like that…

02:57.719 --> 02:58.803
I'm never going back.

02:59.679 --> 03:02.390
If I ever do, it'll be over my dead body.

03:02.473 --> 03:06.060
This premium package
is only for our VIP clients.

03:06.144 --> 03:10.231
We'll finish the massage
with this gold-infused natural oil.

03:10.982 --> 03:11.858
Okay.

03:18.656 --> 03:19.908
How much is this though?

03:21.409 --> 03:23.077
It's the package you've always chosen.

03:25.330 --> 03:26.456
How much was it again?

03:27.665 --> 03:28.499
A hundred?

03:30.460 --> 03:32.795
One… one million won?

03:32.879 --> 03:35.924
Since you added foot care today,
it's 1.2 million.

03:37.425 --> 03:38.259
Hold on.

03:39.135 --> 03:40.845
That's strange. I should be broke.

03:40.929 --> 03:42.889
Come on. I know you're not.

03:42.972 --> 03:45.016
But my dad went
totally bankrupt last year.

03:45.099 --> 03:47.685
Come on.
You must still have a little bit left.

03:47.769 --> 03:50.563
I doubt it. I likely maxed out
my overdraft account too.

03:52.690 --> 03:53.608
I see.

03:54.192 --> 03:55.276
You spent it all.

03:55.360 --> 03:56.736
So you have no money.

03:56.819 --> 04:00.240
Then you won't have any money
either today, tomorrow, or in the future?

04:01.115 --> 04:01.950
That's right.

04:06.871 --> 04:09.123
Then you give me no choice.

04:09.958 --> 04:10.959
Sorry?

04:17.215 --> 04:19.425
If you don't have money,
you'll have to work it off.

04:19.509 --> 04:20.927
That's how the world works.

04:23.846 --> 04:24.973
Hold on.

04:25.056 --> 04:26.599
What is this? Don't! Stop!

04:26.683 --> 04:27.767
In this world,

04:28.601 --> 04:32.397
there are things you have to do
even if you don't want to, Dr. Oh.

04:32.480 --> 04:34.816
For example, earning money.

04:35.733 --> 04:37.694
No, I have money. I do…

04:38.695 --> 04:39.696
Really! I do have money!

04:41.155 --> 04:43.366
No. You don't.

04:43.950 --> 04:45.827
All right. Shall we start
with the kidneys?

04:46.411 --> 04:47.453
-Music.
-Yes, ma'am.

04:49.706 --> 04:52.250
No! Stop!

05:00.466 --> 05:01.426
Stop…

05:02.302 --> 05:03.970
No. Wait.

05:07.223 --> 05:08.808
Not the saw.

05:28.536 --> 05:29.454
Hello?

05:30.913 --> 05:32.415
I'm driving right now.

05:36.252 --> 05:37.920
What was that? Could you repeat…

05:40.006 --> 05:41.758
Ms. Oh Yi-young.

05:41.841 --> 05:44.635
You're currently using
our bank's overdraft account.

05:45.136 --> 05:47.221
It looks like your due date is next week.

05:47.805 --> 05:51.059
We've tried to contact you several times,
but you must've been very busy.

05:53.936 --> 05:54.896
Yes.

05:54.979 --> 05:55.855
A little bit.

05:56.439 --> 05:57.482
I see. Currently,

05:57.565 --> 06:00.485
you can either repay
the overdraft amount of 50 million won

06:00.568 --> 06:01.652
-or--
-Wait.

06:01.736 --> 06:03.029
I used up all 50 million?

06:03.780 --> 06:08.284
The total balance
is negative 46,407,000 won, ma'am.

06:08.367 --> 06:12.997
If immediate repayment is difficult,
you can extend the loan period.

06:13.915 --> 06:14.874
Then I'll do that.

06:14.957 --> 06:16.459
All right, ma'am.

06:17.210 --> 06:20.755
If you bring your certificate
of employment by next week--

06:20.838 --> 06:23.257
I don't have one.

06:23.341 --> 06:26.219
Then what about your previous year's
tax withholding statement?

06:26.302 --> 06:27.720
I don't have that either.

06:27.804 --> 06:29.138
Do you have a job at the moment?

06:31.516 --> 06:34.435
Then, when do you plan on working again?

06:34.519 --> 06:38.231
It's not that I don't want to work.
I just can't.

06:38.314 --> 06:39.649
I tried.

06:40.191 --> 06:42.985
But I don't think
the working environment suits me.

06:43.945 --> 06:44.779
It's too hard.

06:48.157 --> 06:49.659
So it doesn't suit you.

06:53.621 --> 06:55.123
Then, in that case…

06:56.874 --> 06:59.794
Once the due date passes,
and depending on the credit card company,

06:59.877 --> 07:02.380
your card may be suspended
and your limit may be reduced.

07:02.463 --> 07:04.465
As creditor,
the bank may request the courts

07:04.549 --> 07:06.134
for an investigation of assets.

07:06.217 --> 07:07.552
Then assets could be frozen.

07:07.635 --> 07:11.722
And after that, there may be legal action
and seizure of assets, ma'am.

07:17.437 --> 07:20.231
What did you say I needed again?

07:21.566 --> 07:23.651
-A certificate…
-A certificate?

07:24.152 --> 07:25.153
…of employment.

07:25.736 --> 07:26.863
Of employment.

07:27.780 --> 07:29.866
A certificate of employment.

07:29.949 --> 07:31.451
A certificate of employment.

07:45.465 --> 07:48.676
RESIDENT PLAYBOOK

08:06.611 --> 08:08.529
What's taking you so long?

08:15.203 --> 08:16.287
You're going out like that?

08:17.413 --> 08:19.707
Joo-young, these pants are latest--

08:19.790 --> 08:20.917
Right. They're nice.

08:21.918 --> 08:22.919
We'll be late. Let's go.

08:28.424 --> 08:29.425
By the way…

08:30.927 --> 08:32.094
Do I really have to go?

08:32.678 --> 08:33.804
Damn it.

08:33.888 --> 08:36.933
JONGNO YULJE MEDICAL CENTER

08:37.475 --> 08:40.353
At least it feels familiar
since you interned here, right?

08:40.436 --> 08:41.270
I guess.

08:41.938 --> 08:43.314
At least we won't get lost.

08:43.981 --> 08:45.483
Let go of me. I'm not a child.

08:46.776 --> 08:48.152
This isn't my first rodeo.

08:48.236 --> 08:50.446
I need to see you go inside
with my own eyes.

08:51.239 --> 08:53.741
You're smart, so I know you'll do well.

08:53.824 --> 08:56.035
You'll find it fulfilling
and make money too.

08:56.577 --> 08:59.997
Right, you'll even be able
to make friends. How great is that?

09:00.081 --> 09:01.165
Whatever.

09:01.832 --> 09:03.543
Who was it that scammed Dad again?

09:03.626 --> 09:05.878
A friend of 50 years
who stole five billion won.

09:06.712 --> 09:08.506
Good. I'm glad you brought it up.

09:09.131 --> 09:12.343
He's not the only one who went broke.
You did too. You're dirt-poor.

09:12.426 --> 09:14.554
You have no home or car.
Just debts. So shut it.

09:15.596 --> 09:19.141
Still, it's embarrassing
to come back here.

09:20.184 --> 09:22.311
Use your brain for once, will you?

09:22.395 --> 09:24.647
He can't open a hospital for you anymore.

09:24.730 --> 09:25.940
You can't be a director.

09:26.023 --> 09:29.151
And what hospital would take you
after that huge mess you made?

09:29.235 --> 09:32.488
You think you can go to any university
or local hospital there is?

09:33.489 --> 09:35.533
That's why I'm back here.

09:35.616 --> 09:39.161
If it weren't for me, you would've missed
applying for the additional recruitment.

09:39.245 --> 09:41.205
You should be thanking me.

09:42.081 --> 09:43.165
All right.

09:43.791 --> 09:44.959
I'll go in.

09:45.960 --> 09:46.877
Geez.

09:48.045 --> 09:50.881
Just hang in there
until you repay the 50 million won.

09:50.965 --> 09:51.799
After that…

09:54.844 --> 09:57.263
Whatever! We'll talk again
after you pay it back.

09:57.346 --> 10:00.558
You quit before repaying your debt,

10:00.641 --> 10:03.978
and you'll be lying in the morgue.
Got that?

10:07.106 --> 10:09.650
Geez, I can't stand looking at you.
Get in there!

10:12.194 --> 10:13.112
Bye.

10:31.839 --> 10:33.132
You little…

10:38.929 --> 10:40.056
Just one year.

10:40.139 --> 10:42.475
Please just hang in there for one year.

10:55.655 --> 10:57.073
Just a moment!

10:58.866 --> 11:00.201
Wait!

11:03.996 --> 11:05.665
-Going up.
-Thank you.

11:10.002 --> 11:12.046
-We're getting off.
-Excuse me.

11:27.853 --> 11:29.772
It's so nice to see you here.

11:30.564 --> 11:31.440
Sure.

11:32.024 --> 11:34.485
The lounge moved
to the fifth floor last year.

11:34.568 --> 11:36.237
Please pretend you don't know me.

11:36.320 --> 11:39.031
I was just letting you know
since you seemed unaware.

11:39.115 --> 11:40.533
As a fourth-year to a first-year.

11:40.616 --> 11:43.744
You can tell the other first-years.
Don't tell me anything.

11:43.828 --> 11:45.996
It's weirder
that you're making such a fuss.

11:47.248 --> 11:48.249
All right.

11:49.625 --> 11:51.210
Don't complain I didn't help later.

11:51.293 --> 11:52.753
That's never going to happen.

11:59.176 --> 12:00.386
No, to your right.

12:18.696 --> 12:19.989
RESIDENT LOUNGE

12:20.072 --> 12:22.366
AUTHORIZED PERSONNEL ONLY

12:28.456 --> 12:30.291
Yes, I'm on my way.

13:00.196 --> 13:03.073
OB-GYN, FIRST-YEAR RESIDENT LOUNGE
2023 OB-GYN RESIDENT RECRUITMENT

13:26.055 --> 13:27.264
-Good morning.
-Hello.

13:27.348 --> 13:28.557
Hi.

13:28.641 --> 13:30.893
You all look so different
in your lab coats.

13:30.976 --> 13:31.894
Take a seat.

13:35.481 --> 13:36.357
Thank you.

13:36.440 --> 13:38.234
I'm a fourth-year resident, Ku Do-won.

13:38.317 --> 13:40.402
This is third-year resident,
Dr. Ki Eun-mi.

13:40.486 --> 13:42.279
This is second-year resident,
Dr. Cha Da-hye.

13:42.363 --> 13:44.406
They'll be your saviors today.

13:44.490 --> 13:45.324
Say hi.

13:45.407 --> 13:46.659
Hi, guys.

13:47.826 --> 13:50.287
Today's your first day,
so let's do introductions.

13:54.083 --> 13:54.917
What?

13:55.000 --> 13:57.211
Wow, is this real?

13:58.128 --> 13:59.713
It's ancient history, but--

13:59.797 --> 14:01.674
The top student is joining our department?

14:02.258 --> 14:05.052
Which "top" were you referring to?

14:05.135 --> 14:08.055
I was top student in med school
and got the top score on national exams.

14:12.685 --> 14:13.894
I'm Kim Sa-bi.

14:13.978 --> 14:15.521
I read Prof. Seo Jung-min's paper

14:15.604 --> 14:19.149
on "Pre-eclampsia Prediction Algorithm
Using Machine Learning" last March

14:19.233 --> 14:21.360
and became interested
in the OB-GYN department.

14:21.443 --> 14:23.404
And last month, after I read her paper

14:23.487 --> 14:26.740
on "Pregnancy Complications
and Fetal Programming in the Uterus,"

14:26.824 --> 14:28.200
that cemented my decision.

14:29.368 --> 14:31.161
I look forward to working with you.

14:31.245 --> 14:32.872
You're better than your seniors.

14:32.955 --> 14:34.498
She published another paper?

14:35.165 --> 14:36.375
-Beats me.
-Next up…

14:40.296 --> 14:42.047
This has to be a real first.

14:42.131 --> 14:44.675
That's right. It's not common.

14:44.758 --> 14:48.012
You two attended the same high school?
Did you know each other?

14:50.264 --> 14:51.891
We both went to Baejin High School.

14:56.228 --> 14:57.062
Nam-jeong?

14:57.146 --> 14:58.105
Nam-kyung.

14:58.188 --> 15:00.232
Right, Nam-kyung.
We were classmates in junior year.

15:00.316 --> 15:01.901
Classmates in senior year.

15:02.610 --> 15:04.111
You're right. Sorry.

15:05.195 --> 15:06.697
Jung Nam-kyung?

15:07.823 --> 15:08.782
Pyo Nam-kyung.

15:11.952 --> 15:15.289
Dr. Pyo, it looks like you stopped
dying your hair halfway through.

15:15.372 --> 15:17.750
Why? Did you run out of money? Or time?

15:17.833 --> 15:19.168
This is the trend.

15:20.377 --> 15:22.671
If I untie it,
you can't see the dyed part.

15:22.755 --> 15:25.674
So when the professors are around,
I'll keep my hair down.

15:25.758 --> 15:27.718
When they're not, I'll have it tied.

15:27.801 --> 15:29.261
Different styles?

15:29.345 --> 15:31.680
You'll be quite busy.
Okay, introduce yourself.

15:33.599 --> 15:35.684
Hello, I'm Pyo Nam-kyung.

15:36.226 --> 15:40.189
I may look like an uptight city slicker,
but I'm actually pretty easygoing.

15:40.272 --> 15:42.441
I hope we can all get along well.

15:43.067 --> 15:44.526
-All right.
-Thank you.

15:44.610 --> 15:45.903
Next…

15:48.656 --> 15:49.531
Dr. Oh Yi-young.

15:50.658 --> 15:52.993
I'm Oh Yi-young. I'm 28 years old.

15:54.119 --> 15:55.162
That's it.

16:00.084 --> 16:02.044
The thing about Dr. Oh is…

16:02.836 --> 16:05.547
She interned and started
her residency here two years ago,

16:06.382 --> 16:07.883
and then went to a local hospital.

16:09.510 --> 16:11.553
Simply put,
she's repeating a year as a resident.

16:11.637 --> 16:13.472
-I see.
-I see.

16:15.849 --> 16:18.268
Well, she's back now.
That's what matters, right?

16:18.852 --> 16:21.563
You're all in the same year,
so try to get along. Okay?

16:22.731 --> 16:24.233
And lastly…

16:30.280 --> 16:31.240
Yes, it's me.

16:31.323 --> 16:33.242
Dr. Um, your coat is inside out.

16:34.493 --> 16:36.537
No one usually makes that mistake.

16:36.620 --> 16:38.747
-Right.
-Introduce yourself first.

16:40.708 --> 16:43.377
Hello! I'm Um Jae-il,
and I'm 28 years old.

16:43.919 --> 16:45.421
My stage name is Um Jay.

16:45.504 --> 16:47.381
Stage name? Why a stage name?

16:47.464 --> 16:48.507
"Umji"?

16:48.590 --> 16:50.467
Like in the Korean phrase for "thumbs up"?

16:50.551 --> 16:52.761
No. It's Um Jay.

16:52.845 --> 16:55.139
Um. J-A-Y.

16:55.222 --> 16:57.391
-He's our first foreigner, right?
-Yes.

16:57.474 --> 16:58.517
I'm not a foreigner.

16:59.435 --> 17:01.437
-What?
-I'm like a one-hit wonder.

17:02.271 --> 17:03.856
From an old music group.

17:03.939 --> 17:06.400
-I was in an old K-pop idol group--
-That's right!

17:06.483 --> 17:07.943
Cha Eun-woo's group.

17:08.027 --> 17:09.111
No, not that one.

17:09.194 --> 17:11.196
No, it's that actor. What was his name?

17:11.280 --> 17:12.948
-Yim Si-wan. His group.
-Oh, that.

17:13.032 --> 17:14.116
No, not ZE:A either.

17:15.659 --> 17:16.910
We were called HI-BOYZ.

17:17.411 --> 17:18.245
We did this.

17:22.875 --> 17:24.626
Right! You might've seen this one.

17:31.717 --> 17:34.470
Basically, you're saying
you used to be a K-pop idol?

17:34.553 --> 17:37.222
Fine. Say something quick
and wrap it up. I'm busy.

17:37.765 --> 17:38.974
Yes, sir.

17:39.058 --> 17:42.519
I might not be the best at studying,
but I'm good at physical work.

17:42.603 --> 17:45.147
I'll keep going
until the soles of my feet wear out.

17:45.230 --> 17:46.482
I'd appreciate your support.

17:47.399 --> 17:50.152
All right.
Anyways, we're glad you're all here.

17:50.235 --> 17:51.195
Let's give them a hand!

17:51.278 --> 17:52.112
Clap, clap.

17:53.614 --> 17:56.575
Since it's your first day,

17:56.658 --> 17:59.328
our senior residents
will help you a lot today.

17:59.411 --> 18:01.080
But since they're also busy,

18:01.163 --> 18:03.874
let's not ask the same questions
or make the same mistakes twice.

18:03.957 --> 18:04.833
Yes, sir!

18:04.917 --> 18:08.420
But always ask if you don't know something
and check things that are unclear.

18:08.504 --> 18:09.463
-Yes, sir!
-Yes, sir.

18:09.546 --> 18:12.591
If your mistake comes all the way to me,
it means you messed up big time.

18:12.674 --> 18:14.843
So let's hope we don't meet again today.

18:15.636 --> 18:17.221
-Got it?
-Yes, sir!

18:17.304 --> 18:18.889
-Dismissed.
-Dismissed!

18:22.059 --> 18:22.893
Good luck.

18:22.976 --> 18:24.061
Have a nice day.

18:24.144 --> 18:25.020
Goodbye.

18:41.620 --> 18:43.539
I'm heading up to the Gynecology ward.

18:44.373 --> 18:45.207
Good luck.

18:48.544 --> 18:50.379
Right, I have to go to the ward too.

18:50.462 --> 18:51.547
See you later.

18:53.757 --> 18:54.591
Hello.

18:55.676 --> 18:57.469
Hey, I'm a bit disappointed though.

18:57.553 --> 18:59.721
We were the top two students
at Baejin High.

18:59.805 --> 19:00.973
We were archrivals.

19:01.807 --> 19:03.308
We were?

19:04.143 --> 19:05.185
I guess not.

19:09.148 --> 19:11.608
You don't believe what our classmates said

19:11.692 --> 19:13.777
about me following you
to med school, do you?

19:14.278 --> 19:15.445
That's news to me.

19:24.705 --> 19:26.623
-The operating room?
-Yeah.

19:26.707 --> 19:28.917
-Whose surgery?
-Prof. Seo Jung-min's.

19:29.001 --> 19:31.628
Yikes. Surgery on your first day
with Seo Jung-min?

19:33.714 --> 19:35.632
Don't you remember? You interned here.

19:37.009 --> 19:38.093
No, I don't remember.

19:40.053 --> 19:43.348
Hey, I'll let you in on something
since we're old classmates.

19:45.893 --> 19:48.854
They say a notorious endemic disease
is going around here.

19:48.937 --> 19:50.022
The "Bitchy Disease."

19:50.856 --> 19:52.024
Seo Jung-min's terminal.

19:52.107 --> 19:55.110
She tears you down with her words
and eyes over and over again.

19:56.653 --> 19:58.155
-She's that scary?
-Yeah.

19:58.238 --> 20:00.824
If you get on her bad side,
she'll criticize you all day.

20:01.575 --> 20:03.994
She's out to torment us.

20:07.873 --> 20:09.958
You know what her nickname is?

21:04.680 --> 21:05.597
Hello.

21:06.223 --> 21:08.058
So we have a new first-year resident.

21:08.558 --> 21:09.726
Welcome.

21:09.810 --> 21:12.646
Did our junior resident watch
the surgery videos in advance?

21:12.729 --> 21:13.730
I did.

21:13.814 --> 21:16.191
Just your luck
to get me on your first day.

21:16.275 --> 21:17.901
Did you hear that my nickname is

21:18.694 --> 21:20.070
-"The Witch"?
-Yes.

21:23.323 --> 21:24.700
Who told you?

21:24.783 --> 21:26.451
First-year resident Pyo Nam-kyung.

21:27.035 --> 21:29.371
What a helpful colleague she is.

21:32.457 --> 21:36.044
By the way, junior. Isn't your vision
blurry and hazy right now?

21:36.712 --> 21:38.630
-It is.
-You can't see in front of you

21:38.714 --> 21:40.340
and things look out of focus?

21:40.424 --> 21:41.842
Yes, how did you…

21:42.509 --> 21:43.760
How did you know that?

21:43.844 --> 21:46.596
Right? I wonder how.

21:47.222 --> 21:48.140
Ma'am.

21:57.441 --> 21:58.275
Right.

22:00.736 --> 22:01.570
Thank you.

22:01.653 --> 22:03.238
Ma'am, she's been contaminated.

22:08.410 --> 22:11.371
We need to deliver the baby quickly
since it's general anesthesia.

22:11.455 --> 22:14.249
We'll make the incision
right after intubation.

22:14.333 --> 22:15.500
Dr. First-Year.

22:15.584 --> 22:17.127
Pay close attention.

22:17.210 --> 22:18.545
Yes, ma'am.

22:21.715 --> 22:23.467
I'll start the time-out checklist.

22:24.051 --> 22:25.886
Can the anesthesiologist
verify the patient?

22:25.969 --> 22:28.847
Yes, registration number 19210681.

22:28.930 --> 22:30.891
Patient name, Sung Hui-young.

22:30.974 --> 22:33.769
-Diagnosis and procedure?
-Placenta previa totalis.

22:33.852 --> 22:36.688
A low flap transverse cesarean section
will be performed.

22:36.772 --> 22:39.608
-Do we have fetal cord blood sampling?
-No.

22:39.691 --> 22:41.526
-Is everything correct?
-Yes.

22:42.152 --> 22:43.987
-Beginning anesthesia.
-Okay.

22:44.654 --> 22:47.449
SURGERY IN PROGRESS

23:03.090 --> 23:04.174
Richardson retractor.

23:05.258 --> 23:06.551
Meyer forceps.

23:17.813 --> 23:19.815
Pull. One, two, three.

23:22.526 --> 23:23.527
Bladder retractor.

23:24.236 --> 23:25.070
Metzenbaum.

23:34.037 --> 23:34.871
Scalpel.

23:43.171 --> 23:44.297
I'll apply fundal pressure.

23:44.381 --> 23:46.049
APPLYING PRESSURE
ON THE TOP OF THE UTERUS

23:56.101 --> 23:57.269
The baby is out.

23:58.145 --> 23:59.312
Hi!

23:59.396 --> 24:01.523
Time is 10:23 a.m. It's a baby girl.

24:02.941 --> 24:05.152
-Is the baby okay?
-Yes, Apgar score is nine.

24:05.235 --> 24:07.821
Saturation level is good,
and her pulse is over 100.

24:11.908 --> 24:12.742
Hey, junior.

24:13.368 --> 24:15.412
You used two pairs
of gloves on your first day.

24:15.495 --> 24:16.454
What a busy day, right?

24:17.789 --> 24:19.583
Do-won, I'll leave the rest to you.

24:19.666 --> 24:20.584
Yes, ma'am.

24:20.667 --> 24:23.295
-Good work, everyone.
-Thank you.

24:34.306 --> 24:35.599
Was her name Oh Yi-young?

24:35.682 --> 24:37.559
The one who caused trouble
at a local hospital?

24:37.642 --> 24:39.853
Yeah, that's her.
I felt bad for her though.

24:39.936 --> 24:42.022
She had Prof. Seo on her first day.

24:42.105 --> 24:44.024
I think she's already on her bad side.

24:44.107 --> 24:45.734
Geez, what awful luck.

24:46.318 --> 24:47.485
That's just her fate.

24:48.111 --> 24:49.946
And the surgery's over now, right?

24:50.030 --> 24:51.740
That's just how you pass the days.

24:53.867 --> 24:57.037
It's not over.
We're packed with OB surgeries today.

25:00.457 --> 25:02.083
But seriously, what'll she do?

25:02.167 --> 25:04.461
Isn't it obvious? She'll have to bear it.

25:22.020 --> 25:24.147
Make way! She's in labor! Move aside!

25:27.025 --> 25:28.693
Slow down. You're going too fast.

25:29.653 --> 25:31.321
No, hurry up! Quick!

25:31.863 --> 25:34.241
The baby's coming!

25:39.913 --> 25:40.789
Hello?

25:41.623 --> 25:43.541
I'll come up right away.

25:49.005 --> 25:50.006
Where have you been?

25:50.715 --> 25:51.549
Here.

25:53.343 --> 25:54.177
You're the first.

25:55.720 --> 25:56.554
All right.

26:00.517 --> 26:04.020
"I wish you happiness."

26:05.689 --> 26:08.066
I was checking
Mr. Yoon I-sang's biopsy result.

26:08.149 --> 26:09.442
I see.

26:10.318 --> 26:11.236
What is this?

26:12.445 --> 26:13.280
My autograph.

26:15.699 --> 26:17.117
You better not sell that online.

26:17.200 --> 26:20.412
Dr. Um, it's a busy day today.

26:20.495 --> 26:22.580
We don't have time to joke around.

26:22.664 --> 26:24.374
These are Cho Seon-yeong's test results.

26:24.457 --> 26:27.002
And you can check
biopsy results on your computer.

26:27.085 --> 26:28.712
You don't have to ask in person.

26:32.716 --> 26:34.342
I was curious about the result.

26:34.426 --> 26:36.636
I thought I could get it faster in person,

26:37.137 --> 26:38.346
but it wasn't out yet.

26:50.400 --> 26:52.277
No way. Jay's a doctor?

26:52.360 --> 26:55.196
I knew it.
He's just as smart as he is sexy.

26:55.697 --> 26:56.948
Doctor.

26:57.032 --> 26:58.658
Yes, hello.

26:58.742 --> 26:59.659
Hello.

26:59.743 --> 27:03.038
I was told to exercise a lot
after the surgery,

27:03.121 --> 27:04.706
so I've been walking around.

27:05.373 --> 27:07.250
But for some reason,

27:07.334 --> 27:09.961
my chest feels uncomfortable
and my shoulder hurts.

27:10.045 --> 27:11.004
Is this normal?

27:11.087 --> 27:12.881
Could you tell me your name?

27:12.964 --> 27:14.132
Yoon Jung-sun.

27:15.050 --> 27:17.844
My shoulder's been hurting
since this morning.

27:18.470 --> 27:20.347
How should I describe it? My chest

27:21.264 --> 27:22.182
feels tight.

27:22.849 --> 27:25.810
Your shoulder and chest area feel stiff.

27:26.478 --> 27:27.896
And you feel short of breath too?

27:27.979 --> 27:29.356
Yes, that's right.

27:29.939 --> 27:31.524
Is this normal after surgeries?

27:33.860 --> 27:34.736
One moment, please.

27:40.784 --> 27:43.703
Hello, Dr. Cha.
I'm sorry to call you for the fifth time.

27:44.287 --> 27:46.623
I think I found
a case of aortic dissection.

27:46.706 --> 27:47.916
What? What did you say?

27:50.210 --> 27:51.503
A tear in the aorta.

27:51.586 --> 27:52.712
I'm coming now.

27:52.796 --> 27:55.173
-Did she get a chest CT scan?
-Right, a CT scan.

27:55.256 --> 27:57.634
Have you gotten a chest CT scan?

27:57.717 --> 27:59.135
What's that?

27:59.219 --> 28:01.846
Hold on. Who are you talking to right now?

28:01.930 --> 28:04.432
The patient is standing
in front of me right now.

28:06.142 --> 28:07.936
An aortic dissection patient

28:08.812 --> 28:11.523
is standing in front of you?

28:11.606 --> 28:12.982
Yes, she's here right now.

28:13.066 --> 28:14.442
Dr. Um.

28:14.526 --> 28:15.402
Yes, Doctor?

28:15.485 --> 28:17.153
Are you kidding me right now?!

28:17.737 --> 28:18.571
Unbelievable!

28:19.114 --> 28:20.448
FIRST-YEAR

28:21.825 --> 28:23.910
I think being lazy might be better.

28:23.993 --> 28:26.329
He's too eager for his own good.

28:26.413 --> 28:27.455
Isn't that a good thing?

28:27.539 --> 28:28.832
He's always busy.

28:28.915 --> 28:31.960
He meets with patients,
asks questions, and takes notes.

28:32.043 --> 28:34.295
Then he does it over and over again.

28:34.379 --> 28:36.297
But he never gets anything right.

28:36.381 --> 28:38.842
We were also like him once.
Don't you remember last March?

28:38.925 --> 28:42.053
-I don't think I was like that.
-Yeah, you were. I'm a witness.

28:44.013 --> 28:46.683
Still, I'm sure he has
at least one good quality.

28:48.351 --> 28:49.853
He's hard-working.

28:50.812 --> 28:51.730
And his flaw?

28:53.690 --> 28:55.024
He's hard-working.

28:59.362 --> 29:00.572
This too shall pass.

29:00.655 --> 29:02.365
Summer will be here in a flash.

29:08.621 --> 29:10.498
FIRST-YEAR

29:14.377 --> 29:15.962
What is it now, Dr. Um?

29:17.213 --> 29:18.173
So,

29:18.840 --> 29:22.510
we won't know until we have the surgery?

29:22.594 --> 29:23.428
Yes.

29:24.095 --> 29:26.765
If you look at Section 2-1
of the procedure explanation,

29:26.848 --> 29:29.934
after incising the skin,
we'll assess the extent of the illness

29:30.018 --> 29:33.021
in the abdominal cavity and determine
which organs need to be removed.

29:33.980 --> 29:34.814
I see.

29:35.690 --> 29:37.066
Doctor.

29:37.817 --> 29:38.651
It's…

29:40.987 --> 29:42.071
it's not that difficult

29:42.822 --> 29:45.158
of a surgery, is it?

29:48.369 --> 29:52.832
If we find cancer during surgery,
the extent of the surgery may increase.

30:04.344 --> 30:05.178
Excuse me.

30:05.762 --> 30:07.847
Surgery will take 4 to 5 hours
according to textbooks

30:07.931 --> 30:10.892
with approximately
a 30% chance of complications.

30:12.018 --> 30:13.603
Could you please sign here?

30:24.489 --> 30:25.323
I'm sorry.

30:34.999 --> 30:36.584
I caught you right at mealtime.

30:37.210 --> 30:38.294
Enjoy your dinner.

30:44.884 --> 30:48.012
AUTHORIZED PERSONNEL ONLY

31:02.902 --> 31:04.404
Is that too little? Want more?

31:04.487 --> 31:05.405
No, thanks.

31:05.488 --> 31:07.365
The line's long. Keep moving forward.

31:07.448 --> 31:08.908
Spinach?

31:08.992 --> 31:10.702
Go. Grilled short rib patties?

31:10.785 --> 31:11.870
-Five, please.
-Five…

31:12.954 --> 31:13.788
Really?

31:19.127 --> 31:20.545
-Bean sprouts?
-Three.

31:23.381 --> 31:24.966
-Tofu.
-One?

31:31.347 --> 31:34.017
At least you got a meal break
between surgeries today.

31:34.517 --> 31:36.060
Consider yourself lucky.

31:37.312 --> 31:38.271
Eat up.

31:39.188 --> 31:40.732
What time do we get off today?

31:43.276 --> 31:44.611
At this rate…

31:46.112 --> 31:47.614
Gosh, not on time.

31:47.697 --> 31:49.157
Damn it.

31:49.782 --> 31:52.619
Why do we come to work on time
but never leave on time?

31:54.746 --> 31:55.872
Make sure you eat up.

32:07.425 --> 32:08.509
She's bleeding.

32:08.593 --> 32:10.595
What are you doing, junior?

32:10.678 --> 32:12.764
-Kleenex.
-Kleenex?

32:12.847 --> 32:14.390
What's the English word again?

32:14.474 --> 32:15.433
Tissue, please.

32:16.017 --> 32:19.145
There are no tissues
in the operating room. It's gauze.

32:19.228 --> 32:21.272
You're too relaxed for your first day.

32:22.482 --> 32:23.524
I'm sorry.

32:27.028 --> 32:27.862
Cut.

32:35.078 --> 32:36.162
Is that a souvenir?

32:36.829 --> 32:37.747
Throw it away.

32:38.247 --> 32:39.832
Do I have to tell you that too?

32:45.880 --> 32:48.800
Junior, why put it there
when you can throw it away?

32:58.267 --> 33:00.103
What hospital taught you to put it there?

33:00.186 --> 33:01.521
-At Jongno Yulje--
-Hey!

33:03.439 --> 33:06.567
Objects could end up in the patient
if you leave them in the surgical field!

33:06.651 --> 33:07.694
Get rid of it now!

33:28.464 --> 33:30.717
I'll hold it tight
and throw it away later outside.

33:32.760 --> 33:34.637
Take the suture and leave right now.

33:36.472 --> 33:38.975
Get out of the field right now!

33:53.448 --> 33:54.949
Damn it.

34:02.790 --> 34:04.208
I never said you could move.

34:04.292 --> 34:07.128
I told you to stand there
and watch carefully.

34:07.879 --> 34:10.506
-I have eyes in the back of my head.
-Yes, ma'am.

34:11.591 --> 34:12.425
Cut.

34:21.809 --> 34:22.643
Damn it.

34:40.870 --> 34:41.829
Excuse me, Dr. Cha.

34:42.413 --> 34:44.123
Knock, knock. Sorry to bother you.

34:44.207 --> 34:46.209
Come in. What is it now?

34:47.126 --> 34:50.922
I just checked
on patient Lee Suk-ja in Room 1014.

34:51.005 --> 34:52.006
And?

34:53.049 --> 34:54.050
Her BP is normal.

34:54.675 --> 34:55.760
And the JP drain?

35:00.389 --> 35:01.474
I'll go check again.

35:04.477 --> 35:06.729
Sure. Off you go.

35:12.860 --> 35:13.820
Excuse me, Dr. Cha.

35:13.903 --> 35:15.196
Knock, knock.

35:16.155 --> 35:17.406
Back already?

35:20.159 --> 35:21.577
It was just across the hall.

35:22.537 --> 35:26.707
The JP drain has minimal drainage
and the color looks fine.

35:26.791 --> 35:28.292
Okay. Good work.

35:29.085 --> 35:30.086
Dr. Cha.

35:30.711 --> 35:35.049
Patient Kim Min-suk in Room 1012
has clear fluid leaking from her nose.

35:35.842 --> 35:39.804
Post-surgery,
she's had a headache but no fever.

35:40.638 --> 35:42.390
But clear fluid is leaking from her nose.

35:42.473 --> 35:43.558
So?

35:43.641 --> 35:44.851
So perhaps…

35:44.934 --> 35:46.144
Perhaps?

35:49.772 --> 35:51.691
…it's a skull fracture?

35:53.651 --> 35:56.028
First, an aortic dissection.

35:56.112 --> 35:57.905
And now, a skull fracture?

35:58.739 --> 36:00.867
Yes, at least that's what I think it is.

36:02.368 --> 36:07.206
Ms. Kim had surgery yesterday,
so she's been lying in bed all day.

36:07.290 --> 36:10.960
So how could she have
possibly injured her head?

36:11.043 --> 36:12.837
How? Where?

36:13.546 --> 36:14.380
Why?

36:15.464 --> 36:16.632
I can't tell you that,

36:16.716 --> 36:19.802
but a skull fracture can cause
cerebrospinal fluid to leak from the nose.

36:19.886 --> 36:21.095
I learned that in med school.

36:21.179 --> 36:23.681
So I've been checking
her nasal discharge every 30 minutes.

36:23.764 --> 36:25.308
-Dr. Um.
-Yes?

36:25.808 --> 36:27.894
I wasn't going to say this, but…

36:27.977 --> 36:28.936
Don't you ever get

36:29.478 --> 36:30.646
a runny nose?

36:31.397 --> 36:33.649
-I do.
-You do, right?

36:33.733 --> 36:37.737
We all get it from time to time.
I do. You do.

36:37.820 --> 36:39.197
-Ju-yeon?
-Yes?

36:39.280 --> 36:41.115
-Do you get a runny nose?
-I do.

36:41.199 --> 36:42.533
See? Everyone does.

36:42.617 --> 36:46.495
Patients get it.
Doctors get it. Nurses get it.

36:46.579 --> 36:50.666
All of humanity gets runny noses!

36:50.750 --> 36:52.335
For crying out loud!

37:03.512 --> 37:05.514
Are you okay, ma'am?

37:05.598 --> 37:07.266
I'm monitoring you carefully.

37:07.350 --> 37:08.226
Doctor.

37:08.309 --> 37:10.603
You'll have a safe delivery, ma'am.

37:10.686 --> 37:12.813
It's okay. You can count on me.

37:12.897 --> 37:14.398
That's not it.

37:14.482 --> 37:15.691
Sorry?

37:16.317 --> 37:18.527
You're the one
who doesn't seem to be okay.

37:19.320 --> 37:21.239
I'm just really scared too.

37:21.322 --> 37:22.907
I'm sorry.

37:28.120 --> 37:29.413
That was Pyo Nam-kyung, right?

37:29.914 --> 37:31.666
Yeah, I think so.

37:31.749 --> 37:32.959
Where are you headed?

37:35.253 --> 37:36.963
To get this surgical consent form signed.

37:38.631 --> 37:42.343
Among current residents, I think I may be
the best at getting them signed.

37:43.803 --> 37:44.637
Good for you.

37:54.230 --> 37:56.816
Are you saying you won't sign it?

37:57.400 --> 37:58.734
I won't sign it.

38:01.070 --> 38:02.154
Take it back.

38:03.447 --> 38:06.492
Then would you like
to sign it a little later?

38:06.575 --> 38:08.411
I don't want to receive surgery.

38:09.829 --> 38:12.748
But you need to get it.

38:14.125 --> 38:15.751
You need to sign this right now.

38:16.502 --> 38:18.129
Doctor.

38:18.212 --> 38:21.716
May I ask you something?

38:24.302 --> 38:27.680
You doctors are so smart.

38:28.973 --> 38:33.602
There's a bunch of difficult words
written on that consent form,

38:33.686 --> 38:36.522
yet you memorize them all
to explain them to us

38:37.106 --> 38:40.109
and answer any questions we have.

38:41.110 --> 38:42.737
So I have a question.

38:43.988 --> 38:45.239
Why was I…

38:48.451 --> 38:52.705
cursed with this terrible illness?

38:55.416 --> 38:56.292
Sorry?

38:57.251 --> 38:58.085
You see…

38:59.754 --> 39:00.921
I never drank

39:01.547 --> 39:02.798
or smoked.

39:03.382 --> 39:07.970
And I've tried to live
a good, decent life.

39:09.013 --> 39:11.098
I was afraid of getting punished.

39:12.350 --> 39:13.184
So,

39:13.684 --> 39:16.145
why has this happened to me

39:16.979 --> 39:20.232
for the second time now?

39:24.153 --> 39:25.404
Well…

39:27.198 --> 39:28.616
If I knew the reason,

39:29.617 --> 39:31.786
at least I wouldn't feel so wronged.

39:42.671 --> 39:45.174
So, what's the reason? Doctor?

39:49.887 --> 39:52.681
Being a good person

39:54.308 --> 39:57.853
and… cancer recurrence

39:58.771 --> 40:01.065
aren't related.

40:04.276 --> 40:05.236
I see.

40:37.059 --> 40:38.185
Hey! Good news!

40:38.811 --> 40:39.770
A blind date?

40:42.022 --> 40:42.857
Wrong.

40:43.524 --> 40:45.609
This is even better news.

40:45.693 --> 40:47.361
Better? What is it?

40:47.445 --> 40:48.946
Professor Seo

40:50.197 --> 40:51.198
gave us her credit card.

40:51.907 --> 40:53.742
-Why?
-She said, for working hard today,

40:53.826 --> 40:55.453
we can treat ourselves to good food.

40:55.536 --> 40:57.538
What should we eat? What do you want?

40:57.621 --> 40:59.206
I have dinner plans. Sorry.

40:59.290 --> 41:00.958
See you tomorrow. Bye.

41:01.041 --> 41:03.544
Hey, who has dinner plans this late?

41:03.627 --> 41:06.338
I need to return a book.
Let's eat next time.

41:06.422 --> 41:08.883
Isn't that your book?
Where are you returning…

41:22.897 --> 41:24.148
I'm not hungry.

41:26.859 --> 41:27.860
Enjoy the food.

41:29.236 --> 41:30.488
I can't eat alone.

41:32.156 --> 41:34.366
-Let's eat together next time then.
-Okay.

41:35.826 --> 41:36.744
Good luck.

42:21.247 --> 42:23.832
You should've asked.
I could've driven you.

42:32.216 --> 42:34.718
Prof. Seo is always sensitive
on surgery days.

42:35.386 --> 42:38.556
She doesn't mean anything bad by it,
so I hope you understand.

42:40.015 --> 42:41.267
No, just bear it.

42:46.230 --> 42:47.898
You must be very tired.

42:49.358 --> 42:51.068
No hospital talk at home.

42:51.819 --> 42:52.695
All right.

42:54.488 --> 42:57.074
Why do we have to
keep it secret at work that we're…

42:58.242 --> 43:00.244
Is our relationship weird?

43:00.327 --> 43:01.203
What's so weird?

43:01.287 --> 43:03.330
What good would come of it if they knew?

43:06.083 --> 43:07.501
I could quit at any time.

43:07.585 --> 43:09.086
I doubt it'll be anytime soon.

43:09.169 --> 43:11.422
You're wrong.
I could quit tomorrow if I want.

43:11.505 --> 43:12.840
I doubt it.

43:12.923 --> 43:14.925
God! Stop being so annoying.

43:15.467 --> 43:16.594
Geez, you startled me.

43:43.829 --> 43:45.497
Are you serious?

43:48.626 --> 43:49.710
I didn't do anything.

43:53.005 --> 43:54.256
That's my foot, you know?

43:57.885 --> 43:59.011
It wasn't me.

43:59.094 --> 44:00.262
It was a mouse.

44:00.346 --> 44:03.641
-I heard mice are everywhere these days.
-Really? No wonder.

44:04.433 --> 44:05.392
Here, honey.

44:06.226 --> 44:08.437
Have all the expensive things

44:09.063 --> 44:11.231
before your sister
and this fool eat it all.

44:12.399 --> 44:13.734
You should eat up too.

44:13.817 --> 44:16.737
Just watching you eat
is good enough for me.

44:18.113 --> 44:18.989
Seung-won.

44:19.573 --> 44:22.326
Get your heart checked out
at a hospital as soon as possible.

44:22.993 --> 44:25.329
You have to be sick
to still be in love like that.

44:25.412 --> 44:28.165
Hey, I told you
to speak respectfully to him.

44:28.248 --> 44:31.251
Seung-won is older than you, okay?
Don't take your anger out on him.

44:32.419 --> 44:34.588
Do-won, where are your table manners?

44:34.672 --> 44:36.715
Why did you kick her?

44:37.675 --> 44:39.593
You're making Yi-young uncomfortable.

44:41.762 --> 44:43.722
I'm sorry. I guess it was me.

44:44.890 --> 44:47.184
Just consider this
a way of earning your keep.

44:48.352 --> 44:50.646
Do-won, how was she today?

44:50.729 --> 44:51.563
Did she do well?

44:52.147 --> 44:53.816
Did she cause any trouble?

44:54.358 --> 44:55.567
No, she did fine.

44:56.485 --> 44:57.528
She did well.

45:02.199 --> 45:04.576
So today,
in the operating room, Joo-young--

45:04.660 --> 45:05.536
Don't.

45:07.663 --> 45:08.539
Okay.

45:12.251 --> 45:13.502
What happened?

45:15.879 --> 45:18.257
The professor told her
to throw away a piece of suture,

45:18.340 --> 45:20.342
but she didn't know where to put it.

45:20.426 --> 45:22.803
So she went like this, and then--

45:22.886 --> 45:23.929
I told you to stop.

45:26.974 --> 45:28.183
She worked hard.

45:28.267 --> 45:29.268
Don't tell me…

45:30.352 --> 45:32.813
She already fell out of favor
with the professor?

45:32.896 --> 45:35.691
-She can't quit anytime soon.
-Says who?

45:36.984 --> 45:39.069
You can pay back 50 million that quickly?

45:39.153 --> 45:40.779
Is 50 million a joke to you?

45:42.948 --> 45:47.077
Also, you should've spent less
if you didn't have any money.

45:47.161 --> 45:49.955
But you splurged left and right
without any thought.

45:50.038 --> 45:52.958
Ever since you started spending
so recklessly, I saw this coming.

45:53.041 --> 45:55.252
Even if you gave the bank
your entire monthly paycheck,

45:55.335 --> 45:57.504
you'd need to work a year
to pay the principal.

45:57.588 --> 45:59.423
Come to your senses, you brat.

45:59.506 --> 46:00.632
Damn it.

46:01.467 --> 46:04.136
You didn't have to
tell them about my debt.

46:04.845 --> 46:05.679
I'm not eating.

46:05.762 --> 46:08.015
Geez. Do-won, have some hairtail.

46:09.266 --> 46:10.642
If it weren't for Do-won,

46:10.726 --> 46:12.853
you would've never gotten
into such a big hospital.

46:15.355 --> 46:17.357
You told me
about the shortage of applicants.

46:20.110 --> 46:21.195
While we were eating,

46:21.278 --> 46:24.323
I only said our department was short
and was accepting extra applicants.

46:24.907 --> 46:27.576
I didn't know you'd apply though.

46:29.495 --> 46:31.747
I really didn't think you'd get in.

46:35.542 --> 46:38.754
This is all abuse of power,
school ties, and regional ties.

46:38.837 --> 46:39.713
Everything bad.

46:39.796 --> 46:41.215
What power do I have?

46:41.298 --> 46:43.926
If running my mouth over dinner
counts as power…

46:47.221 --> 46:48.347
Does it count?

46:48.430 --> 46:52.434
What school or regional ties do you have?
Who do you think you are?

46:52.518 --> 46:54.811
It was just good timing.

46:54.895 --> 46:57.064
You only got in thanks to your abilities.

46:57.147 --> 46:59.274
Don't baby her.
That's how she ended up like this.

46:59.358 --> 47:00.651
Who babied me?

47:00.734 --> 47:02.110
Mom and Dad.

47:02.611 --> 47:03.904
And who else? No one.

47:03.987 --> 47:06.156
Grandma. Our aunts and uncle.
There are tons!

47:07.115 --> 47:08.158
Ku Do-won speaking.

47:08.992 --> 47:11.537
You're handing over Ms. Eun Sang-mi to me?

47:12.204 --> 47:13.789
Okay. I'll come right away.

47:15.624 --> 47:17.793
Do-won, at least finish your meal.

47:23.298 --> 47:24.800
I need to go to the hospital.

47:25.300 --> 47:26.260
Again?

47:26.343 --> 47:28.512
A fellow on vacation asked for a favor.

47:29.846 --> 47:30.681
Here.

47:34.226 --> 47:36.812
Dr. Oh, I hope to see you tomorrow.

47:38.105 --> 47:38.939
Gosh.

47:39.606 --> 47:41.483
He can't even eat in peace.

47:42.109 --> 47:44.027
I don't think he's slept well in days.

47:44.111 --> 47:46.154
I told you this job wasn't worth it.

47:47.155 --> 47:49.116
Geez, you little…

47:55.872 --> 47:58.000
Check the lab results on the EMR.

47:59.042 --> 48:00.294
You see that monitor?

48:01.295 --> 48:04.089
Monitor the baby's heart rate
and check for uterine contractions.

48:04.172 --> 48:05.841
Notify me if anything seems off.

48:06.758 --> 48:08.135
Make sure to call me, okay?

48:10.387 --> 48:12.139
-Have you been up all night?
-Yeah.

48:13.390 --> 48:15.892
If you're unsure, ask the nurses.

48:15.976 --> 48:16.852
Okay.

48:16.935 --> 48:18.687
I'm heading to the operating room.

48:19.771 --> 48:21.982
-I'm going to be alone?
-You want my company?

48:22.649 --> 48:24.276
Gosh. No.

48:28.780 --> 48:30.324
Ms. Lee Young-seon is

48:31.199 --> 48:32.618
Professor Seo's patient.

48:33.952 --> 48:36.330
Damn it. The Witch again?

48:36.413 --> 48:39.583
Monitor her carefully. We're all dead
if we miss any deceleration.

48:43.587 --> 48:45.756
I'm always stuck with Seo Jung-min.

48:49.801 --> 48:50.636
Doctor!

48:53.889 --> 48:56.224
There's no doctor here.

48:56.975 --> 48:59.728
Doctor! Could you please come here?

48:59.811 --> 49:01.355
There's no one here.

49:03.106 --> 49:03.940
Doctor?

49:08.445 --> 49:09.488
Yes, coming.

49:12.866 --> 49:14.034
It's a little cold.

49:15.077 --> 49:15.911
Damn it.

49:16.536 --> 49:18.872
Of all the times,
why are you on vacation now?

49:19.915 --> 49:21.667
To say it myself

49:23.126 --> 49:25.212
would be too embarrassing.

49:27.047 --> 49:29.049
No one cared when I mentioned your name.

49:30.592 --> 49:31.677
The doctor in charge?

49:35.013 --> 49:36.181
I see.

49:36.973 --> 49:37.808
Okay.

49:38.392 --> 49:39.267
Bye.

49:40.894 --> 49:42.396
Doctor! One moment.

49:43.021 --> 49:44.064
Over here.

49:45.649 --> 49:46.525
So…

49:49.152 --> 49:50.404
Here.

49:52.531 --> 49:53.532
Doctor.

49:53.615 --> 49:56.076
Thank you so much.

49:57.703 --> 50:01.832
NOT THE SAME BOYFRIEND AS BEFORE

50:01.915 --> 50:02.749
Look…

50:04.292 --> 50:05.877
It's my second time.

50:06.878 --> 50:07.963
But it's a secret.

50:15.178 --> 50:17.305
Okay. I understand.

50:17.389 --> 50:18.223
Honey.

50:18.807 --> 50:20.267
Honey!

50:20.350 --> 50:21.476
Gosh, I'm…

50:21.560 --> 50:23.103
I'm so scared.

50:23.729 --> 50:27.107
I don't know how others
can give birth so smoothly.

50:27.190 --> 50:29.234
What am I going to do?

50:29.317 --> 50:30.777
I'm really nervous too.

50:31.403 --> 50:33.822
Doctor, will we be expecting soon?

50:33.905 --> 50:35.866
Is the baby okay?

50:35.949 --> 50:39.453
Well, she's not dilated at all yet.

50:39.536 --> 50:42.289
The process would be faster
if this was her second or third time…

50:44.583 --> 50:45.959
But it's her first.

50:47.335 --> 50:49.463
So it might take more time.

50:49.546 --> 50:52.674
Let me ask the professor,
and I'll get back to you.

50:54.551 --> 50:56.344
Thank you, Doctor.

50:56.428 --> 50:57.429
Thank you.

50:58.263 --> 50:59.806
Also, if she's had a C-section before…

51:02.225 --> 51:03.351
or a natural birth…

51:04.060 --> 51:06.688
Then things might be different.

51:06.772 --> 51:08.648
But since this is her first delivery,

51:09.149 --> 51:11.943
please let me know
if she's in a lot of pain.

51:12.027 --> 51:13.278
Okay, thank you.

51:14.321 --> 51:15.155
Thank you.

51:16.156 --> 51:17.032
Wait, Doctor.

51:29.336 --> 51:30.212
Are you done?

51:32.756 --> 51:34.007
Yeah. Eat up.

51:38.887 --> 51:41.014
What a weird fellow.

51:41.097 --> 51:43.934
I only notified 30 minutes late.
Why chew me out for it?

51:45.227 --> 51:48.605
And who goes on vacation in March anyway?

51:51.107 --> 51:53.235
You might as well
just eat with your hands.

51:54.110 --> 51:55.612
Who bought this?

51:55.695 --> 51:57.739
A patient's husband
gave it to me as a thank you.

51:57.823 --> 52:00.575
What's there to thank
a lowly first-year for?

52:00.659 --> 52:02.244
Are you sure it wasn't for a professor?

52:04.538 --> 52:05.705
What did you do today?

52:06.623 --> 52:08.625
Did you do something special?

52:08.708 --> 52:11.169
Nothing much. Just what I was told to do.

52:11.253 --> 52:12.254
I see.

52:13.004 --> 52:14.589
I guess you were lucky then.

52:15.632 --> 52:17.425
Guys, can I ask you something?

52:17.509 --> 52:19.553
Ask away. I'll tell you everything.

52:22.389 --> 52:24.474
She's a recurrent ovarian cancer patient,

52:24.558 --> 52:26.393
but she won't sign
the surgical consent form.

52:26.476 --> 52:27.602
How do I persuade her?

52:27.686 --> 52:30.230
Pass it to a senior resident.
That's what they're there for.

52:31.523 --> 52:34.442
I should still try to solve it myself.

52:34.526 --> 52:35.360
Here!

52:36.403 --> 52:39.865
Ask Prof. Ryu Jae-hui if it's related
to recurrent ovarian cancer.

52:39.948 --> 52:42.367
That's not something
I can ask a professor about.

52:42.868 --> 52:44.244
That'll hurt my pride.

52:45.203 --> 52:46.913
I've asked him 16 times.

52:48.832 --> 52:50.250
Hey, has it been 30 minutes?

52:50.333 --> 52:52.002
Urine. I need to check her urine.

52:54.170 --> 52:55.005
How disgusting.

52:59.217 --> 53:00.468
What now?

53:03.638 --> 53:04.806
Yes, Doctor?

53:05.432 --> 53:07.601
Okay, I'll be right there. Goodbye.

53:09.644 --> 53:10.478
Bye.

53:19.237 --> 53:20.488
I'm on OB duty right now.

53:29.664 --> 53:30.498
Hello?

53:33.835 --> 53:35.670
I have to do that?

53:39.466 --> 53:41.468
Okay, I'll be there.

54:06.326 --> 54:08.370
This is it.

54:16.169 --> 54:17.128
Ma'am.

54:17.212 --> 54:20.507
This could be
very uncomfortable and painful.

54:20.590 --> 54:21.591
Please excuse me.

54:33.186 --> 54:35.063
Notify for active labor
if it's 4 cm or more.

54:35.146 --> 54:37.190
Notify for full dilation
if it's totally dilated.

54:37.273 --> 54:38.942
Check for amniotic sac ruptures.

54:45.615 --> 54:46.658
What on earth?

54:46.741 --> 54:48.410
Why? Why already?

54:48.493 --> 54:49.452
Sorry?

54:51.454 --> 54:52.288
She's…

54:52.998 --> 54:53.873
She's all full.

54:53.957 --> 54:56.292
FULL DILATION OF THE CERVIX

54:57.252 --> 55:00.088
I'll call the professor.
She's suddenly all full so…

55:00.171 --> 55:02.674
What did you say? She's what?

55:02.757 --> 55:05.343
She's all full.
Ms. Lee Young-seon is at full dilation.

55:07.637 --> 55:08.763
Hi, this is Seo Jung-min.

55:08.847 --> 55:11.349
Get the current patient
out of the delivery room right now.

55:11.433 --> 55:13.393
Another patient needs to give birth first.

55:28.408 --> 55:31.494
An all-full patient
didn't receive an epidural,

55:31.578 --> 55:34.164
but she's calm enough to ask how I'm doing

55:35.165 --> 55:36.666
with a big smile on her face.

55:38.126 --> 55:39.085
I'm sorry.

55:40.628 --> 55:43.339
The only thing full here is my rage.

55:46.468 --> 55:47.385
I'm sorry.

55:48.553 --> 55:50.638
Ma'am, I just checked.

55:50.722 --> 55:52.182
And you're only 2 cm dilated.

55:52.265 --> 55:53.933
I see.

55:54.017 --> 55:55.435
Let's wait a bit more.

55:56.227 --> 55:59.522
Our first-year resident
must've been very eager to meet the baby.

55:59.606 --> 56:00.857
She was too hasty.

56:03.693 --> 56:06.279
March is really fun, isn't it?

56:11.367 --> 56:13.119
Where did all the residents go?

56:15.580 --> 56:16.623
Here's one.

56:17.373 --> 56:19.209
No, I mean doctors.

56:21.795 --> 56:24.714
Dr. Ku, this is unacceptable.

56:25.298 --> 56:26.174
I'm sorry.

56:26.800 --> 56:28.343
Take better care of the first-years.

56:29.219 --> 56:30.053
Got that?

56:30.136 --> 56:31.513
Yes, I understand.

56:42.816 --> 56:43.775
Yes, Doctor?

56:45.318 --> 56:46.778
You still haven't gotten it?

56:47.946 --> 56:48.863
I'll go.

57:03.211 --> 57:05.130
All those patients
had successful surgeries.

57:05.964 --> 57:08.299
They're doing so well
after being discharged.

57:10.051 --> 57:14.097
I know you're strong enough
to overcome this.

57:19.686 --> 57:20.895
Did she sign it?

57:20.979 --> 57:21.855
Yeah.

57:24.315 --> 57:26.776
She must've been distraught
over the recurrence.

57:27.402 --> 57:28.736
She just needed some time.

57:30.613 --> 57:32.115
You were one step ahead of me.

57:32.198 --> 57:34.033
I'd figured out how to get her to sign.

57:34.117 --> 57:35.785
-There's a way to do that?
-Yes.

57:36.369 --> 57:38.288
Berek &amp; Hacker's Gynecologic Oncology.

57:38.371 --> 57:39.581
It's in this book.

57:40.790 --> 57:42.709
There's a chapter
called "Communication Skills."

57:42.792 --> 57:44.794
"Remove any obstacles
between you and the patient."

57:44.878 --> 57:46.921
"Sit at eye level
within an appropriate distance."

57:47.005 --> 57:49.924
"And quickly offer tissues when they cry."

57:50.008 --> 57:51.009
That's what you did.

57:51.843 --> 57:55.138
I wanted to do the same
and get it signed quickly.

57:56.055 --> 57:57.932
I didn't know that was in the book.

58:02.187 --> 58:04.022
You were worried
she wouldn't get the surgery.

58:04.939 --> 58:05.773
Well…

58:07.817 --> 58:10.403
Darn it. I wanted to
get it signed under my name.

58:11.029 --> 58:12.322
Too bad.

58:16.534 --> 58:18.244
At least she's having the surgery.

58:18.828 --> 58:19.704
That's good.

58:20.288 --> 58:21.289
You're right, but…

58:21.873 --> 58:23.541
If she'd signed it on the first day,

58:23.625 --> 58:26.085
I wouldn't have wasted time
looking for this useless stuff.

58:26.169 --> 58:28.546
I could've processed things more quickly.

58:28.630 --> 58:31.007
I wanted to get all the consent forms
by 6:00 p.m. today

58:31.090 --> 58:33.343
so I could notify the professor first.

58:34.177 --> 58:35.678
-Sa-bi.
-Yes?

58:36.638 --> 58:39.140
Are you trying to come in first place
at getting consent forms?

58:39.891 --> 58:41.142
What's the point of that?

58:42.185 --> 58:45.897
You can get praised at home or school
for coming in first place,

58:46.439 --> 58:47.690
but this is a hospital.

58:48.733 --> 58:50.652
Here, instead of your own desires,

58:51.236 --> 58:53.238
it's where you put your patients first.

58:54.572 --> 58:56.241
Even medical students know that.

58:57.242 --> 58:59.702
But if you had to look it up
and still didn't understand,

59:02.038 --> 59:03.540
it really was a waste of time.

59:06.417 --> 59:07.252
See you.

59:28.773 --> 59:29.607
Dr. Cha.

59:31.317 --> 59:32.151
What is it?

59:32.986 --> 59:34.946
It's Ms. Yeong Bo-mi in Room 1019.

59:35.488 --> 59:38.032
Her urine output has been low
since this morning.

59:39.200 --> 59:40.076
So?

59:43.830 --> 59:46.666
There was significant blood loss
during yesterday's surgery,

59:46.749 --> 59:48.751
and her urine is dark.

59:48.835 --> 59:51.129
What was the urine output
in the last four hours?

59:51.713 --> 59:52.547
Well…

59:55.550 --> 59:57.135
I'll go check.

59:57.218 --> 59:59.012
Around 80 cc.

59:59.679 --> 01:00:02.015
It was about 20 cc per hour
during the early morning.

01:00:03.057 --> 01:00:04.434
I wasn't really sure,

01:00:05.143 --> 01:00:09.188
so I checked by the hour
from 4:00 a.m. to 3:00 p.m.

01:00:09.272 --> 01:00:12.483
Her vitals were okay,
and the JP drain looked fine.

01:00:12.567 --> 01:00:16.070
But I requested a CBC just in case.

01:00:17.155 --> 01:00:19.782
Did you say from 4:00 a.m.?

01:00:20.658 --> 01:00:21.743
Yes, ma'am.

01:00:24.454 --> 01:00:27.707
In conclusion,
I think the patient is dehydrated.

01:00:29.125 --> 01:00:33.880
I'm wondering
if fluid hydration would be a solution.

01:00:38.843 --> 01:00:39.969
Do that then,

01:00:40.637 --> 01:00:41.971
Dr. Um.

01:00:42.555 --> 01:00:43.848
Yes, ma'am. Understood.

01:00:45.183 --> 01:00:46.392
Where are you going now?

01:00:46.476 --> 01:00:48.144
Let me explain it to her first!

01:00:48.227 --> 01:00:51.147
Type up the prescription first, please…

01:00:56.486 --> 01:00:57.445
Okay.

01:00:59.614 --> 01:01:02.241
Nurse, I put in the prescription
for Ms. Yeong.

01:01:02.325 --> 01:01:03.159
Okay.

01:01:09.749 --> 01:01:12.460
FIRST-YEAR

01:01:14.003 --> 01:01:16.047
FIRST-YEAR UM JAE-IL

01:01:22.178 --> 01:01:24.847
Please tell me everything is fine.

01:01:26.099 --> 01:01:27.266
Everything is fine.

01:01:30.770 --> 01:01:31.604
In that case,

01:01:32.647 --> 01:01:34.982
tell me everything will be fine as well.

01:01:36.567 --> 01:01:37.985
I can't promise you that.

01:01:43.700 --> 01:01:45.368
Who is it this time?

01:01:51.165 --> 01:01:53.000
This seems really strange to me too.

01:01:54.043 --> 01:01:55.920
She's all full. I think the baby's coming.

01:01:56.003 --> 01:01:58.548
-Ma'am, please stay calm…
-I checked, and she's all full.

01:01:59.382 --> 01:02:00.633
She's in pain too.

01:02:01.175 --> 01:02:02.802
It's really different this time.

01:02:03.469 --> 01:02:06.097
Doctor, it hurts too much!

01:02:06.180 --> 01:02:08.182
Everyone's either
delivering babies or in surgery.

01:02:08.266 --> 01:02:09.267
I'm the only one here.

01:02:09.350 --> 01:02:10.476
But she's all full!

01:02:10.560 --> 01:02:11.644
Are you sure?

01:02:12.186 --> 01:02:14.021
You know what all full is, right?

01:02:14.105 --> 01:02:16.232
I'm positive!
I can even see the baby's hair!

01:02:16.899 --> 01:02:18.401
Can't you please come now?

01:02:18.484 --> 01:02:20.778
If you're wrong again, Prof. Seo will…

01:02:20.862 --> 01:02:23.281
That's what you're worried about?
Tell her to come right now!

01:02:26.659 --> 01:02:28.327
Hurry!

01:02:28.411 --> 01:02:31.122
Take her to the delivery room.
I'll be there in three minutes. Now.

01:02:31.205 --> 01:02:32.457
Okay.

01:02:33.166 --> 01:02:35.001
-We're moving to the delivery room.
-Okay.

01:02:35.084 --> 01:02:37.920
Ma'am, breathe in short bursts.

01:02:38.004 --> 01:02:38.880
Don't push.

01:02:39.630 --> 01:02:41.132
Just hold on a little longer.

01:02:42.008 --> 01:02:42.884
Doctor.

01:02:44.510 --> 01:02:46.262
This is…

01:02:46.804 --> 01:02:49.724
This is my first time,
so I don't really know, but…

01:02:50.349 --> 01:02:52.018
This is really a first for me.

01:02:52.101 --> 01:02:53.102
What?

01:02:55.354 --> 01:02:57.857
Professor, Ms. Lee Young-seon
is all full and at Station 3.

01:02:57.940 --> 01:02:59.275
You need to come right away.

01:02:59.358 --> 01:03:01.694
I'm coming now.
But why didn't you call sooner?

01:03:02.278 --> 01:03:03.738
I'm sorry. I missed it.

01:03:03.821 --> 01:03:06.908
If it looks like the baby's coming,
handle the delivery in the meantime.

01:03:06.991 --> 01:03:07.867
Yes, ma'am.

01:03:08.659 --> 01:03:09.535
Hurry.

01:03:09.619 --> 01:03:11.078
Hang in there, ma'am.

01:03:11.162 --> 01:03:12.747
To Delivery Room 2, please.

01:03:14.791 --> 01:03:17.210
Doctor, I think the baby is coming.

01:03:17.293 --> 01:03:19.003
Not yet, ma'am.

01:03:21.798 --> 01:03:23.382
I can't hold it in anymore!

01:03:24.592 --> 01:03:26.636
No! Don't!

01:03:27.637 --> 01:03:29.472
No! Hold on!

01:03:30.139 --> 01:03:31.974
Stop! Gloves!

01:04:41.502 --> 01:04:42.336
She delivered.

01:05:08.571 --> 01:05:09.488
What's that sound?

01:05:10.281 --> 01:05:12.199
That's not my patient's baby, right?

01:05:12.283 --> 01:05:13.159
It's not, right?

01:05:14.160 --> 01:05:15.995
This can't be happening, can it?

01:05:35.389 --> 01:05:37.475
SURGERY IN PROGRESS

01:05:39.727 --> 01:05:42.521
Sometimes, babies come out
quicker than expected.

01:05:42.605 --> 01:05:44.565
But you hardly have any tears.

01:05:44.649 --> 01:05:46.317
And the baby is crying well.

01:05:46.400 --> 01:05:48.527
Everything is fine, so don't worry.

01:05:48.611 --> 01:05:51.155
I see. I'm okay.

01:05:51.822 --> 01:05:52.657
Congratulations.

01:05:54.033 --> 01:05:58.037
I feel bad for making that doctor
go through such a hard time.

01:05:59.246 --> 01:06:00.164
I'm sorry.

01:06:03.918 --> 01:06:05.753
-Can you finish up here?
-Yes, Professor.

01:06:07.254 --> 01:06:09.382
You did well, ma'am.

01:06:10.257 --> 01:06:11.592
Thank you.

01:06:11.676 --> 01:06:13.302
Dr. Oh Yi-young!

01:06:16.472 --> 01:06:17.556
Here we are again.

01:06:19.141 --> 01:06:20.142
I'm sorry.

01:06:21.310 --> 01:06:23.604
My patient couldn't even
make it to the delivery room

01:06:23.688 --> 01:06:26.023
and gave birth
in the middle of the hallway.

01:06:26.857 --> 01:06:27.733
You see…

01:06:29.610 --> 01:06:32.113
This wasn't her first baby,
so the labor came quicker--

01:06:32.196 --> 01:06:34.490
It doesn't matter
if it was her first or not.

01:06:34.573 --> 01:06:36.367
Even first-timers can go
into labor quickly

01:06:36.450 --> 01:06:37.868
in rapid labor conditions.

01:06:38.786 --> 01:06:42.873
Babies can come out suddenly,
unexpectedly, and at any given time.

01:06:42.957 --> 01:06:44.208
Don't you know that?

01:06:44.709 --> 01:06:46.961
Do you know what your mistake was today?

01:06:51.716 --> 01:06:54.010
I made two big mistakes.

01:06:54.093 --> 01:06:55.052
First,

01:06:55.845 --> 01:06:58.848
I didn't monitor the patient carefully
since she was only 2 cm dilated.

01:06:59.473 --> 01:07:00.558
Second,

01:07:00.641 --> 01:07:03.644
I failed to monitor progress,
so I missed the active labor phase

01:07:03.728 --> 01:07:06.022
and couldn't predict the time of delivery.

01:07:06.647 --> 01:07:09.984
Those were my two biggest mistakes.

01:07:11.402 --> 01:07:12.945
At least you know.

01:07:14.280 --> 01:07:15.448
I'm sorry.

01:07:16.323 --> 01:07:17.324
Be sure to go

01:07:18.701 --> 01:07:20.411
and say a prayer of thanks today.

01:07:22.329 --> 01:07:23.205
For what?

01:07:23.289 --> 01:07:25.541
For the mother and her baby being okay.

01:07:27.710 --> 01:07:28.544
Okay.

01:07:29.837 --> 01:07:31.422
Make one more mistake.

01:07:33.049 --> 01:07:33.883
Then…

01:07:36.552 --> 01:07:39.221
I'll show you
what the real Witch looks like.

01:07:51.150 --> 01:07:53.694
FIRST-YEAR RESIDENT LOUNGE
OB-GYN

01:07:55.154 --> 01:07:56.781
Today's tarot reading was terrible.

01:07:58.741 --> 01:08:00.618
Tomorrow's horoscope is awful too.

01:08:03.996 --> 01:08:05.206
Does anyone have a power bank?

01:08:19.178 --> 01:08:20.054
Here you go.

01:08:20.137 --> 01:08:22.306
Look at you, Um Jae-il.

01:08:25.184 --> 01:08:26.727
I feel drained too.

01:08:27.812 --> 01:08:29.063
How could I not be?

01:08:29.146 --> 01:08:31.023
My input and output are both at zero.

01:08:31.107 --> 01:08:32.775
An electrolyte imbalance.

01:08:32.858 --> 01:08:34.235
You had cake earlier.

01:08:35.277 --> 01:08:39.657
So your input isn't at zero.
I don't know about your output though.

01:08:42.284 --> 01:08:43.869
It's just an expression.

01:08:44.495 --> 01:08:46.831
And I had that cake

01:08:47.832 --> 01:08:49.083
ages ago.

01:08:49.583 --> 01:08:51.585
AI programs show more warmth than you do.

01:08:56.715 --> 01:08:58.217
They said we can go home now.

01:08:58.300 --> 01:08:59.135
Yes!

01:09:01.262 --> 01:09:03.139
I doubt you'll get
any sleep tonight, Yi-young.

01:09:03.222 --> 01:09:05.933
They say you weep and think
of your mom on your first delivery.

01:09:06.016 --> 01:09:08.602
Our fellow interns would call
their moms right after delivery.

01:09:08.686 --> 01:09:10.146
Did you call yours too?

01:09:10.938 --> 01:09:11.814
No, I couldn't.

01:09:11.897 --> 01:09:14.567
For an experienced patient
to go from 2 cm to full dilation,

01:09:14.650 --> 01:09:15.943
it takes three to four hours.

01:09:16.026 --> 01:09:19.655
So why did it progress so quickly?
Were there risk factors for rapid labor?

01:09:19.738 --> 01:09:21.157
That's what you're curious about?

01:09:21.240 --> 01:09:24.243
Did the baby really feel slippery
as if you might drop it?

01:09:24.326 --> 01:09:26.245
I don't know.
All I did was hold my hands out.

01:09:26.328 --> 01:09:27.705
Right?

01:09:27.788 --> 01:09:30.124
Honestly, you can't say
she delivered the baby.

01:09:30.207 --> 01:09:32.918
It just came out.
You can't count that as her first.

01:09:33.544 --> 01:09:34.753
Of course, it does.

01:09:35.713 --> 01:09:37.798
I'm jealous. Congratulations, Yi-young.

01:09:37.882 --> 01:09:39.133
Right. See you tomorrow.

01:09:39.633 --> 01:09:40.676
Hey.

01:09:40.759 --> 01:09:43.512
Still, doesn't it feel better
to struggle together than alone?

01:09:43.596 --> 01:09:47.266
That's exactly why I didn't go solo.
I'm meant to be in a group. So--

01:09:47.349 --> 01:09:49.643
-Can this wait until tomorrow?
-Hear me out for a second.

01:09:49.727 --> 01:09:51.437
I discovered something really amazing.

01:09:51.520 --> 01:09:52.646
Check this out.

01:09:52.730 --> 01:09:53.939
There's an O in Oh Yi-young.

01:09:54.023 --> 01:09:55.399
There's a B in Kim Sa-bi.

01:09:55.482 --> 01:09:57.526
There's a G in Pyo Nam-kyung.

01:09:57.610 --> 01:09:58.444
I spell it with a K.

01:09:59.028 --> 01:10:00.321
And I'm Um Jay.

01:10:00.404 --> 01:10:02.364
There's a Y in Jay.

01:10:04.491 --> 01:10:06.410
As in OB-GYN.

01:10:06.493 --> 01:10:08.329
Totally mind-blowing.

01:10:09.205 --> 01:10:10.331
Isn't that incredible?

01:10:13.876 --> 01:10:14.752
I guess not.

01:10:16.587 --> 01:10:17.504
Fine.

01:10:18.464 --> 01:10:19.381
I'm so hungry.

01:10:19.465 --> 01:10:21.300
You haven't eaten, right?
Aren't you starving?

01:10:22.426 --> 01:10:24.261
Want to grab dinner before we go?

01:10:25.012 --> 01:10:26.472
-I have plans--
-I'm busy--

01:10:27.348 --> 01:10:28.515
-Next time.
-Next time.

01:10:31.060 --> 01:10:33.020
Sure. Let's eat next time.

01:10:33.103 --> 01:10:35.272
-I have plans too.
-I see.

01:10:35.356 --> 01:10:36.523
-See you tomorrow.
-Bye.

01:10:37.316 --> 01:10:38.484
-Thanks.
-Sure.

01:10:39.818 --> 01:10:40.653
Bye.

01:10:57.253 --> 01:10:58.087
My goodness.

01:10:58.796 --> 01:10:59.880
She's running.

01:11:00.464 --> 01:11:01.632
What's gotten into her?

01:11:04.885 --> 01:11:06.804
I've never seen Yi-young run before.

01:11:06.887 --> 01:11:08.847
She woke up on her own this morning.

01:11:08.931 --> 01:11:10.599
Oh, no. I think she's late.

01:11:10.683 --> 01:11:12.351
That never bothered her before.

01:11:12.434 --> 01:11:13.686
You're right about that.

01:11:14.395 --> 01:11:16.146
They say you mature
after delivering a baby.

01:11:16.230 --> 01:11:18.774
-I guess it's true.
-You know what Do-won said?

01:11:18.857 --> 01:11:21.860
He wouldn't have chosen OB-GYN
if he hadn't seen a delivery as an intern.

01:11:22.444 --> 01:11:23.279
Really?

01:11:23.362 --> 01:11:26.115
Does that mean Yi-young
will become a doctor like him?

01:11:26.740 --> 01:11:28.158
That may be a bit difficult.

01:11:29.994 --> 01:11:30.828
Right?

01:11:33.789 --> 01:11:35.833
Yi-young is a really transparent kid.

01:11:35.916 --> 01:11:37.584
I can always read her face.

01:11:38.627 --> 01:11:40.713
She seems totally into OB-GYN work now.

01:11:40.796 --> 01:11:43.048
I think she'll really settle down
this time around.

01:11:43.132 --> 01:11:46.719
It's only been three days.
I don't know if she'll last forever.

01:11:46.802 --> 01:11:49.930
But I'm sure she'll have
the common decency to last for a month.

01:11:50.639 --> 01:11:52.182
Gosh. Just a month?

01:11:57.187 --> 01:12:00.524
You probably didn't hear about this
since you were on vacation.

01:12:00.607 --> 01:12:02.609
It's a legendary story of a baby's birth.

01:12:03.152 --> 01:12:07.114
Our first-year resident here
delivered a baby in the hallway.

01:12:07.948 --> 01:12:09.867
I see. It was you.

01:12:12.036 --> 01:12:14.079
-Yes.
-Prof. Seo must've chewed you out.

01:12:14.955 --> 01:12:17.541
Well, first-years can make mistakes.

01:12:18.292 --> 01:12:22.004
Gosh, Jung-min always had a nasty temper.

01:12:23.213 --> 01:12:26.675
Everyone who witnesses
a delivery for the first time says,

01:12:26.759 --> 01:12:28.886
"Professor, I think OB is my calling."

01:12:28.969 --> 01:12:29.970
They all say that.

01:12:32.723 --> 01:12:33.724
Really?

01:12:33.807 --> 01:12:35.184
You're not interested, Dr. Oh?

01:12:35.267 --> 01:12:36.852
Not really.

01:12:40.189 --> 01:12:42.691
I guess it's still
a bit too early to know.

01:12:43.567 --> 01:12:46.987
I don't let just anyone do this, you know.

01:12:47.696 --> 01:12:51.325
But since today's surgery went well
and to celebrate your first delivery,

01:12:51.408 --> 01:12:52.910
why don't you do the last suture?

01:12:52.993 --> 01:12:54.036
That's okay, ma'am.

01:12:55.037 --> 01:12:57.247
I see. Is it because you're scared?

01:12:57.331 --> 01:12:59.166
I'll be here watching. It's okay.

01:12:59.249 --> 01:13:00.334
I'm okay. Really.

01:13:11.887 --> 01:13:14.807
I'll… I'll do it next time.

01:13:15.516 --> 01:13:16.350
Is she serious?

01:13:16.433 --> 01:13:17.476
It's a joke.

01:13:17.559 --> 01:13:18.852
She's just kidding, Doctor.

01:13:20.145 --> 01:13:22.272
Professor, I'll finish up.

01:13:22.356 --> 01:13:25.109
You can leave it to me and get some rest.

01:13:27.152 --> 01:13:28.237
Good work.

01:13:28.320 --> 01:13:29.405
Thank you.

01:13:40.707 --> 01:13:42.793
-Good work today.
-Thank you.

01:13:43.627 --> 01:13:44.670
Excuse me.

01:13:44.753 --> 01:13:45.587
Yes?

01:13:45.671 --> 01:13:48.006
What was the name
of that first-year resident?

01:13:48.841 --> 01:13:50.134
Dr. Oh Yi-young.

01:13:54.555 --> 01:13:56.890
I see. Oh Yi-young.

01:13:57.891 --> 01:14:00.144
So that's her name.

01:14:03.230 --> 01:14:04.314
Good work today.

01:14:04.398 --> 01:14:06.483
Yes, you too.

01:14:47.816 --> 01:14:50.861
THANKS TO OUR SPECIAL GUEST, RA MI-RAN,
SSANGMUN'S OWN CHEETAH LADY

01:14:50.944 --> 01:14:54.198
RESIDENT PLAYBOOK

01:14:54.281 --> 01:14:56.325
The warning signs
have been showing for a while.

01:14:56.408 --> 01:14:58.744
The residents' escape and escaping.

01:14:58.827 --> 01:15:01.079
I may be broke, but I still have my pride.

01:15:01.163 --> 01:15:03.290
I don't think
you're cut out to be a doctor.

01:15:03.373 --> 01:15:04.541
They're all the same.

01:15:04.625 --> 01:15:05.876
Please, just this once.

01:15:05.959 --> 01:15:07.920
Look, Dr. First-Year. This isn't right.

01:15:08.003 --> 01:15:09.296
Use your head.

01:15:10.297 --> 01:15:12.466
Why do patients keep complaining
about the dressings?

01:15:12.549 --> 01:15:13.967
-Well…
-What is it?

01:15:14.468 --> 01:15:16.512
Hey! How will you manage as a doctor?

01:15:17.137 --> 01:15:19.181
Is this what you call
being "in the doghouse"?

01:15:19.264 --> 01:15:20.390
You're quitting as a doctor?

01:15:20.474 --> 01:15:23.352
Why do you do your job like such a fool?

01:15:23.435 --> 01:15:24.269
What did you say?

01:15:24.353 --> 01:15:26.647
Let's not lie to each other from now on.

01:15:26.730 --> 01:15:29.566
It's just that things go wrong
whenever she's involved.

01:15:29.650 --> 01:15:30.692
Say it.

01:15:31.193 --> 01:15:34.446
By the way, they're your own patients.
How do you not know them?

01:15:34.530 --> 01:15:36.198
You're an enemy, not a colleague.

01:15:36.281 --> 01:15:38.825
Yi-young, you're 50 million in debt.
Don't forget that.

01:15:38.909 --> 01:15:40.410
How about you try something else?

01:15:40.494 --> 01:15:43.038
I don't think I can be a doctor.

01:15:43.121 --> 01:15:44.498
Tell her to handle it herself.

01:15:45.165 --> 01:15:46.375
I can't do this anymore.

01:15:47.042 --> 01:15:48.544
What am I doing here?

01:15:49.044 --> 01:15:52.172
It's the perfect weather for running away.

01:15:59.805 --> 01:16:01.807
Subtitle translation by: Sooji Kim
